BEGIN IMMEDIATE;

-- v0.36 gives the deities that had only evidence cards a located story to
-- open. Greek: the Homeric Hymns to Apollo, Hermes and Aphrodite (a series
-- with the existing Hymn to Demeter), the Titans' children in the Theogony,
-- Artemis and Dionysus in Apollodorus and Ares in the Iliad. Norse: long
-- versions of the Gylfaginning creation and of Sif's hair, and Thor and
-- Hrungnir. Egyptian: the Bentresh Stela, the Tale of Two Brothers,
-- Hatshepsut's birth cycle and the Memphite Theology. Ugaritic: Baal's
-- palace. Sumerian: Inana and Ebih. Chinese: Leigong in the Lunheng. Every
-- section keeps its own anchor claim with evidence at the same locator;
-- broken passages are named, not filled in.

