('story.greek.hymn_apollo','Homeric Hymns, Part 2: Apollo — Leto''s wandering and Delphi','荷马颂歌 · 第二部 致阿波罗：勒托的漂泊与德尔斐','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','勒托怀着宙斯的孩子，走遍了爱琴海四周的土地，却没有一处敢接纳她，因为人人都怕那个将要出生的神。只有贫瘠多石的得洛斯岛，在勒托发誓之后答应了她。赫拉把生育女神厄勒梯亚留在奥林波斯，勒托在岛上阵痛了九天九夜，直到众女神派伊里斯用一条金项链把厄勒梯亚请来。勒托抱住一棵棕榈树，生下了阿波罗；阿波罗一尝到神食就挣开襁褓，说竖琴和弯弓是他的心爱之物。后半首讲阿波罗寻找建立神谕所的地方：他被泉水女神泰尔福萨骗到帕尔纳索斯山下的克里萨，在那里奠下神庙的地基，射死了替赫拉抚养提丰的母龙，又化身海豚把一船克里特人带来做他的祭司。','Leto, carrying Zeus''s child, wanders all the lands around the Aegean, but none dares to receive her, for all fear the god to be born. Only rocky Delos agrees, once Leto has sworn an oath. Hera keeps Eileithyia, goddess of birth, on Olympus, and Leto labours nine days and nights until the goddesses send Iris with a golden necklace to bring her. Clasping a palm tree, Leto bears Apollo, who at his first taste of ambrosia bursts his swaddling bands and claims the lyre and the curved bow. The second half tells how Apollo seeks a site for his oracle: tricked by the spring nymph Telphusa into going to Crisa below Parnassus, he lays the foundations of his temple, shoots the she-dragon that had reared Typhaon for Hera, and in the form of a dolphin brings a shipload of Cretans to be his priests.','["希腊", "荷马颂歌", "勒托", "阿波罗", "得洛斯", "德尔斐", "系列", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',12,651,'依据 Evelyn-White 英译《荷马颂歌》第三首，按诗行顺序讲述。这首颂歌通常被分为“得洛斯的阿波罗”（第1–178行）与“皮托的阿波罗”（第179–546行）两部分，可能原本是两首诗；本篇按传世的完整顺序讲述。颂歌只称那条母龙为“母龙”，“皮同”这个名字出自后世作家。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.hymn_hermes','Homeric Hymns, Part 3: Hermes — Maia''s child','荷马颂歌 · 第三部 致赫尔墨斯：迈亚的孩子','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','仙女迈亚住在库勒涅山的幽暗山洞里，宙斯趁赫拉熟睡时夜里去找她，她生下了赫尔墨斯。这个孩子清晨出生，中午就用一只乌龟的壳做成了竖琴，傍晚就偷走了阿波罗的五十头牛：他让牛倒着走，自己穿上树枝编的鞋，在阿尔甫斯河边生火宰了两头牛，再像一阵雾一样从锁孔钻回摇篮。迈亚责备他，他却说要做盗贼的首领。阿波罗循着古怪的蹄印找到山洞，赫尔墨斯装成刚出生的婴儿，矢口否认；两兄弟一直吵到宙斯面前，宙斯哈哈大笑，命他们和好。最后赫尔墨斯弹起竖琴，阿波罗听得入迷，便用牛群换下了竖琴，两位神从此结为朋友。','The nymph Maia lived in a shadowy cave on Mount Cyllene; Zeus came to her by night while Hera slept, and she bore Hermes. Born at dawn, by midday he had made a lyre from a tortoise shell, and by evening he had stolen fifty of Apollo''s cattle, driving them backwards while he wore sandals woven of twigs; by the Alpheus he made fire and slaughtered two cows, then slipped back through the keyhole like mist into his cradle. Maia scolded him, and he answered that he would be prince of thieves. Apollo followed the strange tracks to the cave; Hermes curled up like a newborn and denied everything, and the brothers took their quarrel to Zeus, who laughed and bade them make peace. At last Hermes played the lyre, Apollo was enchanted, and traded the cattle for it; the two gods became friends for ever.','["希腊", "荷马颂歌", "迈亚", "赫尔墨斯", "阿波罗", "竖琴", "系列", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',12,652,'依据 Evelyn-White 英译《荷马颂歌》第四首，按诗行顺序讲述。颂歌里的诗行编号据希腊文本；个别诗行在传本中有缺损或重复，本篇只讲述连贯可读的部分。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.hymn_aphrodite','Homeric Hymns, Part 4: Aphrodite — the goddess and the herdsman','荷马颂歌 · 第四部 致阿佛洛狄忒：女神与牧人','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','阿佛洛狄忒能让众神、凡人和一切鸟兽产生爱欲，只有三位女神的心她无法改变：爱战争和手艺的雅典娜、爱弓箭和山林的阿耳忒弥斯，以及发誓永远做处女、在每户人家的正中享受尊荣的赫斯提亚。阿佛洛狄忒常常让宙斯爱上凡间女子，宙斯便反过来让她爱上在伊达山放牛的特洛伊王子安喀塞斯。她在帕福斯梳妆以后来到伊达山，扮成弗里吉亚的公主走进他的小屋。醒来以后她现出真身，告诉吓坏了的安喀塞斯，他们会有一个儿子叫埃涅阿斯；她讲了宙斯带走伽倪墨得斯，讲了黎明女神厄俄斯为情人提托诺斯求得了不死却忘了求不老，最后托山中的仙女抚养孩子，并警告他永远不要说出孩子的母亲是谁。','Aphrodite stirs desire in gods, men and all creatures; only three goddesses she cannot bend — Athena who loves war and handicraft, Artemis who loves the bow and the mountains, and Hestia, sworn to maidenhood and honoured at the centre of every house. Because Aphrodite often made Zeus love mortal women, Zeus in turn made her love Anchises, a Trojan prince herding cattle on Ida. Adorned at Paphos, she came to Ida and entered his hut disguised as a Phrygian princess. Afterwards she revealed herself to the terrified Anchises and told him they would have a son, Aeneas; she told how Zeus carried off Ganymede, and how Eos won immortality for her beloved Tithonus but forgot to ask for youth; then she entrusted the child to the mountain nymphs and warned Anchises never to say who his mother was.','["希腊", "荷马颂歌", "阿佛洛狄忒", "赫斯提亚", "厄俄斯", "安喀塞斯", "系列", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',11,653,'依据 Evelyn-White 英译《荷马颂歌》第五首，按诗行顺序讲述。颂歌把赫斯提亚称为克洛诺斯的第一个孩子，又因宙斯的意旨成为最小的孩子，这是指她被克洛诺斯第一个吞下、最后一个吐出（参见《神谱》）。女神与安喀塞斯的结合只按原诗简略讲述。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.titans_children','The children of the Titans: light, wind, sleep and death (after Hesiod''s Theogony)','提坦的子女：光、风、睡与死（据赫西俄德《神谱》）','GENEALOGICAL_ACCOUNT','civ.greek','赫西俄德的《神谱》除了讲宙斯怎样夺得王位，还记下了许多很少被单独讲述的神的家世。混沌生出幽暗厄瑞玻斯和黑夜，黑夜又生出明亮的埃忒耳和白昼赫墨拉；大地和天空生下十二位提坦，其中有克利俄斯、许珀里翁和忒亚；黑夜独自生下睡神许普诺斯和死神塔纳托斯。忒亚为许珀里翁生下太阳、月亮塞勒涅和黎明厄俄斯，海的女儿欧律比亚为克利俄斯生下阿斯特赖俄斯、帕拉斯和珀耳塞斯；厄俄斯和阿斯特赖俄斯生下了风和星辰，帕拉斯和斯梯克斯生下了胜利与力量，斯梯克斯因为第一个投奔宙斯而成了众神的誓言。福柏的女儿阿斯忒里亚嫁给珀耳塞斯，生下了受宙斯尊崇的赫卡忒。诗的后半还写到夜与昼在铜门槛前交替、睡与死住在大地边缘的屋子里，以及厄俄斯为提托诺斯生下的儿子们。','Besides telling how Zeus won his throne, Hesiod''s Theogony records the families of many gods seldom told on their own. Chaos brings forth Erebus and Night; Night bears bright Aether and Day; Earth and Heaven bear the twelve Titans, among them Crius, Hyperion and Theia; Night alone bears Sleep and Death. Theia bears Sun, Moon and Dawn to Hyperion; Eurybia, daughter of Sea, bears Astraeus, Pallas and Perses to Crius; Dawn and Astraeus bring forth the winds and stars; Pallas and Styx bring forth Victory and Strength, and Styx, first to come to Zeus''s side, becomes the oath of the gods. Phoebe''s daughter Asteria marries Perses and bears Hecate, whom Zeus honours above all. Later the poem shows Night and Day passing at a bronze threshold, Sleep and Death dwelling at the edge of the world, and the sons Dawn bore to Tithonus.','["希腊", "神谱", "提坦", "黑夜", "睡与死", "黎明", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',13,655,'依据 Evelyn-White 英译赫西俄德《神谱》，按诗行顺序选取讲述这些神的段落；宙斯与提坦之战、提丰之战等已收入其他故事，这里不重复。《荷马颂歌》等其他作品中关于同一些神的不同家世（如月亮是帕拉斯之女、太阳的母亲叫欧律法厄萨）只在相应章节注明，不并入《神谱》。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.artemis_library','Artemis: twelve tales of the huntress (after the Library)','阿耳忒弥斯：狩猎女神的十二个故事（据《书库》）','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','阿波罗多洛斯的《书库》没有为阿耳忒弥斯写一个连贯的故事，却在许多神话里让她出场。按书中的顺序读下来，就能看到这位女神的全貌：她先于阿波罗出生，还帮母亲接生了弟弟；她和阿波罗一起射死了侵犯勒托的巨人提堤俄斯；她杀死了巨人猎手俄里翁和自以为能攻上天的阿洛伊代兄弟；俄纽斯和阿德墨托斯忘了给她献祭，一个招来了卡吕冬的野猪，一个在婚房里看见满屋的蛇；赫拉克勒斯射伤她的圣鹿，被她当面责备；偷看她沐浴的阿克泰翁被自己的猎狗撕碎；夸耀子女比勒托多的尼俄柏失去了女儿；违背誓言的卡利斯托被变成熊射死；在奥里斯，她用逆风困住希腊舰队，最后从祭坛上带走了伊菲革涅亚。','Apollodorus''s Library gives Artemis no single connected story, yet she appears in many myths. Read in the book''s order they give a full picture of the goddess: born before Apollo, she helps her mother deliver her brother; with Apollo she shoots the giant Tityus who assaulted Leto; she slays the giant hunter Orion and the Aloadae who thought to storm heaven; Oeneus and Admetus forget her sacrifices — one brings down the Calydonian boar, the other finds his bridal chamber full of snakes; Heracles wounds her sacred hind and is rebuked to his face; Actaeon, who saw her bathing, is torn apart by his own hounds; Niobe, who boasted of more children than Leto, loses her daughters; Callisto, who broke her vow, is turned into a bear and shot; and at Aulis she holds the Greek fleet with contrary winds and at last snatches Iphigenia from the altar.','["希腊", "书库", "阿耳忒弥斯", "狩猎", "勒托", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',10,656,'依据弗雷泽英译阿波罗多洛斯《书库》及《摘要》，按卷节顺序把阿耳忒弥斯出场的段落连起来讲述。《书库》常并列不同的说法（如俄里翁和卡利斯托之死的原因），本篇照录这些分歧，不替它们作出选择；刻律涅亚牝鹿一段也收在“希腊英雄”系列的赫拉克勒斯部分。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.dionysus_library','Dionysus: the twice-born god (after the Library)','狄俄倪索斯：两次出生的神（据《书库》）','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','宙斯爱上了忒拜公主塞墨勒，赫拉骗塞墨勒请宙斯以向赫拉求婚时的样子来见她。宙斯驾着雷电到来，塞墨勒在恐惧中死去，宙斯从火中救出六个月的胎儿，缝进自己的大腿，到了足月才生下狄俄倪索斯。孩子先由伊诺和阿塔玛斯当作女孩抚养，赫拉让这对夫妇发了疯；宙斯又把他变成小山羊，交给倪萨的仙女们。长大以后，狄俄倪索斯发现了葡萄，被赫拉逼疯，流浪到埃及和叙利亚，在弗里吉亚得到瑞亚的净化，学会了秘仪。色雷斯国王吕枯耳戈斯驱逐了他，最后被马撕碎；忒拜国王彭透斯阻止酒神的狂欢，被自己的母亲撕碎。他雇了第勒尼安海盗的船，海盗想把他卖掉，他让桅杆变成蛇，海盗跳海变成了海豚。最后他从冥府带回母亲，让她以堤俄涅之名升上天空；在阿提卡，伊卡里俄斯从他那里学会了酿酒，却因此丧命。','Zeus loved Semele, princess of Thebes, and Hera tricked her into asking Zeus to come to her as he came when he wooed Hera. Zeus came with thunder and lightning; Semele died of fright, and Zeus snatched the six-month child from the fire, sewed it in his thigh and bore Dionysus at full term. The child was reared as a girl by Ino and Athamas, whom Hera drove mad; Zeus turned him into a kid and gave him to the nymphs of Nysa. Grown, Dionysus discovered the vine, was driven mad by Hera, wandered to Egypt and Syria, was purified by Rhea in Phrygia and learned the rites. Lycurgus of Thrace drove him out and was in the end torn apart by horses; Pentheus of Thebes opposed the revels and was torn apart by his own mother. Hiring a Tyrrhenian pirate ship, he turned the mast into snakes when the pirates meant to sell him, and they leapt into the sea and became dolphins. At last he brought his mother up from Hades and ascended with her, renamed Thyone; and in Attica Icarius learned winemaking from him and died for it.','["希腊", "书库", "狄俄倪索斯", "塞墨勒", "葡萄酒", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',10,657,'依据弗雷泽英译阿波罗多洛斯《书库》第三卷 3.4.3–3.5.3 与 3.14.7，按卷节顺序讲述。彭透斯、吕枯耳戈斯等情节在欧里庇得斯《酒神的伴侣》、《荷马颂歌·致狄俄倪索斯》等作品中有不同的讲法，本篇只讲《书库》；被撕碎等暴力情节保留结果，不渲染细节。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.greek.ares_iliad','Ares: the war god before Troy (after the Iliad)','阿瑞斯：特洛伊城下的战神（据《伊利亚特》）','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.greek','《伊利亚特》里的战神阿瑞斯站在特洛伊人一边，却总是在神的较量中吃亏。雅典娜把他领出战场，阿佛洛狄忒受伤后借他的马车逃回奥林波斯；狄俄涅讲起他曾被巨人兄弟关在铜罐里十三个月。阿波罗召唤他，他化作凡人鼓舞特洛伊人，和赫克托耳并肩冲杀，连狄俄墨得斯也只好后退。赫拉和雅典娜驾车出征，宙斯准许雅典娜去对付他；雅典娜戴上冥王的隐身盔，引导狄俄墨得斯的长矛刺进阿瑞斯的腹部，战神发出九千、一万人一样的吼叫，逃回天上向宙斯诉苦，却被父亲骂作“最可恨的神”。后来他的儿子阿斯卡拉福斯战死，他要下去报仇，又被雅典娜夺下盔甲拦住。最后众神亲自参战，雅典娜用一块界石把他打倒在地，阿佛洛狄忒扶着呻吟的他离开战场。','In the Iliad Ares, god of war, fights for the Trojans but keeps losing to other gods. Athena leads him out of the battle; Aphrodite, wounded, borrows his chariot to flee to Olympus; Dione recalls how giant brothers once kept him in a bronze jar for thirteen months. Roused by Apollo, he urges on the Trojans in mortal shape and storms beside Hector until even Diomedes gives way. Hera and Athena drive out, and Zeus lets Athena set upon him: wearing the cap of Hades, she guides Diomedes'' spear into Ares'' belly, and the war god bellows like nine or ten thousand men, flees to heaven to complain to Zeus, and is called by his father the most hateful of the gods. Later his son Ascalaphus falls, and Athena strips his armour to stop him going down for vengeance. At last, when the gods themselves join battle, Athena fells him with a boundary stone and Aphrodite leads him groaning from the field.','["希腊", "伊利亚特", "阿瑞斯", "雅典娜", "特洛伊战争", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',12,658,'依据巴特勒英译荷马《伊利亚特》，按卷次顺序把阿瑞斯出场的段落连起来讲述；诗行编号据希腊文本。阿瑞斯与阿佛洛狄忒被赫菲斯托斯用网罩住的故事出自《奥德赛》第八卷，属于另一部作品，这里不并入。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.norse.thor_hrungnir','Thor and Hrungnir: the stone-hearted giant and three-year-old Magni','索尔与赫朗格尼尔：石心巨人与三岁的马格尼','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.norse','奥丁骑着八足马斯莱普尼尔来到巨人国，与最强壮的巨人赫朗格尼尔赛马，一路追进了阿斯加尔德。众神请赫朗格尼尔喝酒，他喝醉了，扬言要把瓦尔哈拉搬回巨人国、杀光众神，只留下芙蕾雅和希芙。索尔回来后，巨人约他在边境的格约特纳加尔德决斗。巨人们用黏土造了一个九里高的泥巨人，给它装上一颗母马的心；赫朗格尼尔自己有一颗三角形的石心，拿着石盾和磨石。索尔的仆人提亚尔菲骗巨人站到盾牌上，索尔的锤子与巨人的磨石在空中相撞，磨石碎裂，一块嵌进索尔的头里，锤子砸碎了巨人的头颅。巨人倒下时一条腿压在索尔的脖子上，众神都抬不动，只有索尔三岁的儿子马格尼把它推开。最后，女巫格罗亚为索尔念咒取石，却因为听到丈夫奥尔万迪尔快要回来的好消息，高兴得忘了咒语，磨石从此留在了索尔的头里。','Óðinn rides Sleipnir to Jötunheimr and races Hrungnir, strongest of the giants, all the way into Ásgarðr. The gods give Hrungnir drink; drunk, he boasts that he will carry Valhalla off to Jötunheimr and kill all the gods except Freyja and Sif. When Thor returns, the giant challenges him to a duel at Grjótúnagarðar on the border. The giants build a clay giant nine leagues tall and give it a mare''s heart; Hrungnir himself has a three-cornered heart of stone and carries a stone shield and a whetstone. Thor''s servant Thjálfi tricks the giant into standing on his shield; Thor''s hammer and the giant''s whetstone meet in the air, the whetstone shatters, a piece lodges in Thor''s head, and the hammer crushes the giant''s skull. Hrungnir falls with his leg across Thor''s neck; none of the gods can lift it until Thor''s three-year-old son Magni throws it off. At last the seeress Gróa chants to draw out the stone, but forgets her spells for joy at the news that her husband Aurvandill is coming home, and the whetstone stays in Thor''s head.','["北欧", "诗语法", "索尔", "马格尼", "巨人", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',11,661,'依据斯诺里《埃达·诗语法》第17章（布罗德尔英译本的章节编号）逐段讲述。斯诺里讲这个故事，是为了解释吟唱诗人图约多尔夫的《秋长诗》等诗中的典故，诗中的细节与散文有时不同，这里只讲散文。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.egyptian.bentresh_khonsu','Khonsu''s journey: the tale of the Bentresh Stela','孔苏远行：本特蕾什石碑的故事','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.egyptian','一块立在卡纳克孔苏神庙旁的石碑讲道：拉美西斯二世在那哈林接受各国的贡品，巴赫坦国王把长女献给了他，她成为王后奈芙鲁拉。后来巴赫坦派来信使，说王后的妹妹本特蕾什病了。国王派生命之屋的书吏前去，书吏发现公主被一个精灵附身，无能为力。巴赫坦国王再次求援，这一次要的是一位神。国王来到底比斯的“孔苏·奈弗尔霍特普”神像前，请他转向另一尊“驱邪者孔苏”，让驱邪者孔苏带着他的护佑远行巴赫坦。神像走了一年零五个月，一到公主身边，她立刻痊愈；附身的精灵向神致敬，请求与神和国王一同过节后离去。巴赫坦国王舍不得放神回去，把神像留了三年零九个月，直到梦见神化作一只金鹰飞向埃及，才把神像连同厚礼送回底比斯。','A stela set up beside the temple of Khonsu at Karnak tells how Ramesses II, receiving tribute in Naharin, was given the eldest daughter of the prince of Bakhtan, who became Queen Neferure. Later a messenger came: the queen''s younger sister Bentresh was ill. The king sent a scribe of the House of Life, who found the princess possessed by a spirit he could not overcome. The prince of Bakhtan asked again — this time for a god. The king went before Khonsu-in-Thebes-Neferhotep and asked him to turn to the image called Khonsu-the-Provider, who drives out disease demons, and send him to Bakhtan with his protection. The god travelled a year and five months; as soon as he reached the princess she was well, and the spirit greeted the god and asked for a feast with him and the prince before it departed. The prince, loath to let the god go, kept him three years and nine months, until he dreamed of the god flying as a golden falcon toward Egypt; then he sent the image back to Thebes with rich gifts.','["埃及", "孔苏", "底比斯", "治病", "神像", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',11,671,'依据卢浮宫藏本特蕾什石碑（C 284）按碑文顺序讲述。石碑把故事放在拉美西斯二世时代，但它的语言和出土地点表明它写成于很晚的时期（波斯或托勒密时代，学界仍有争论），并没有拉美西斯时代的记载可以印证；本篇把它当作一个托古的宗教故事讲述，不作史实断言。“巴赫坦”在哪里也不确定。碑文中的年份与日期据现代学者的释读。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.egyptian.two_brothers','The Tale of Two Brothers: Bata, the Valley of the Pine and Pre-Harakhti','两兄弟的故事：巴塔、松树谷与拉-哈拉赫提','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.egyptian','阿努比斯和巴塔是一对亲兄弟，哥哥有家有妻，弟弟像儿子一样替他耕田放牛，连牛都会告诉他哪里的草最好。嫂子诱惑巴塔遭到拒绝，反诬他施暴，哥哥拿着长矛躲在牛棚门后要杀他，母牛们警告了巴塔。巴塔逃跑时向拉-哈拉赫提祈祷，太阳神在兄弟之间造出一条满是鳄鱼的河。天亮后巴塔说出真相，以自残明志，前往松树谷，把心放在松树的花上；哥哥回家杀了不忠的妻子。九柱神在松树谷遇见巴塔，拉-哈拉赫提命克努姆为他造了一个妻子，七位哈托尔却预言她将死于刀下。大海卷走她的一缕香发送到法老那里，法老派人把她接来，她泄露了巴塔的秘密，松树被砍倒，巴塔死去。哥哥看见啤酒起沫，找了三年才找到那颗心，把弟弟救活。巴塔先后化作公牛和两棵鳄梨树，最后借一片木屑重生为法老的儿子，登上王位，审判了妻子，让哥哥做了王储。','Anubis and Bata are brothers; the elder has house and wife, and the younger works his fields and herds his cattle like a son — the cattle even tell him where the grass is best. The elder''s wife tries to seduce Bata, is refused, and accuses him falsely; Anubis waits behind the byre door with a spear, and the cows warn Bata. Fleeing, Bata prays to Pre-Harakhti, who sets a water full of crocodiles between the brothers. At dawn Bata tells the truth, maims himself to prove it, and goes to the Valley of the Pine, placing his heart on the pine''s flower; Anubis goes home and kills his faithless wife. The Ennead meets Bata in the valley, and Pre-Harakhti has Khnum fashion him a wife, though the Seven Hathors foretell she will die by the knife. The sea carries a scented lock of her hair to Pharaoh, who has her brought to him; she betrays Bata''s secret, the pine is cut, and Bata dies. Anubis, seeing his beer froth, searches three years for the heart and revives his brother. Bata becomes a bull, then two persea trees, and at last, through a splinter, is reborn as Pharaoh''s son, takes the throne, judges his wife and makes his brother crown prince.','["埃及", "纸草", "两兄弟", "拉-哈拉赫提", "克努姆", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',14,672,'依据大英博物馆藏多比尼纸草（EA 10183），按纸草顺序讲述。故事中的哥哥与神同名，叫阿努比斯，巴塔也是一位古老的神名，学者认为这个故事与上埃及某地关于这两位神的传说有关，但在纸草中他们是凡人兄弟。诱惑、自残与杀妻等情节只讲结果，不渲染细节。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.egyptian.hatshepsut_divine_birth','Daughter of Amun: the divine birth of Hatshepsut','阿蒙的女儿：哈特谢普苏特的神圣诞生','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.egyptian','在底比斯西岸代尔拜赫里的哈特谢普苏特神庙里，一组浮雕讲述了这位女法老的神圣出身。众神之王阿蒙-拉在众神面前宣布，他要生下一位未来的统治者；托特向他推荐了图特摩斯一世的王后雅赫摩斯，又引他来到王后的寝宫。阿蒙化作国王的模样，王后被神的香气唤醒，看见了神的真身，神为将要出生的女儿取名“与阿蒙结合的哈特谢普苏特”。阿蒙吩咐陶工之神克努姆在陶轮上塑造孩子和她的卡，蛙头女神赫凯特把生命之符递到她们面前。托特向王后报喜，克努姆和赫凯特领她走进产房，孩子诞生了。哈托尔把婴儿献给阿蒙，阿蒙称她为心爱的女儿和两地之王，众女神和神牛哺育她，托特把孩子和她的卡呈给阿蒙，众神为她定下了千百万年的寿命。','In Hatshepsut''s temple at Deir el-Bahari on the west bank of Thebes, a cycle of reliefs tells the divine origin of this woman king. Amun-Re, king of the gods, announces before the gods that he will beget a future ruler; Thoth commends to him Ahmose, queen of Thutmose I, and leads him to her chamber. Amun takes the king''s form; the queen wakes at the god''s fragrance and sees him in his true form, and the god names the coming daughter Khenemet-Amun Hatshepsut. Amun bids the potter god Khnum shape the child and her ka on his wheel, while the frog goddess Heqet holds out the sign of life. Thoth announces the birth to the queen, Khnum and Heqet lead her to the birth chamber, and the child is born. Hathor presents the infant to Amun, who greets her as his beloved daughter and king of the Two Lands; goddesses and divine cows nurse her; Thoth presents the child and her ka to Amun, and the gods fix her lifetime at millions of years.','["埃及", "阿蒙", "哈特谢普苏特", "神圣诞生", "克努姆", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',10,673,'依据代尔拜赫里神庙中层柱廊北侧的诞生浮雕与题记，按画面顺序讲述；场景的划分与编号据现代学者（布鲁纳）的整理，本篇只标出能核对的编号。这组浮雕是宣扬王权合法性的宗教图像，不作史实断言；浮雕中哈特谢普苏特的形象在图特摩斯三世时被凿毁，阿蒙的形象在阿赫那吞时被破坏，部分题记残缺，残缺处不补写。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.egyptian.memphite_theology','Ptah creates by heart and tongue: the Memphite Theology','普塔用心与舌创造世界：孟菲斯神学','CREATION_ACCOUNT','civ.egyptian','公元前八世纪，库施王朝的法老沙巴卡在孟菲斯的普塔神庙里发现一卷被虫蛀坏的古书，命人把它重新刻在一块石板上。石上的文字先讲大地之神盖布怎样裁决荷鲁斯与塞特之争：起初把埃及一分为二，后来把全部遗产都给了荷鲁斯，荷鲁斯在孟菲斯统一了两地，而孟菲斯的主神普塔被称为“塔特恩”，统一两地之王。接着是著名的“神学”部分：一切神都以普塔的形式出现，阿图姆是在普塔的心中和舌上成形的；心想出一切，舌说出一切，众神、城市、食物和一切技艺都由普塔的话语而生。普塔造完万物后安息了，众神进入用木、石、泥做成的身体里。最后讲奥西里斯在水中淹溺，伊西斯和奈芙蒂斯把他救上孟菲斯的岸边，他进入大地，荷鲁斯在父亲的怀抱中成为上下埃及之王。','In the eighth century BCE the Kushite pharaoh Shabaka found in the temple of Ptah at Memphis an old book eaten by worms and had it carved anew on a stone slab. The text first tells how Geb, god of the earth, judged between Horus and Seth: at first he divided Egypt between them, then gave the whole inheritance to Horus, who united the Two Lands at Memphis — and Ptah, god of Memphis, is called Ta-tenen, the king who unites the land. Then comes the famous ''theology'': all the gods appear as forms of Ptah, and Atum took shape in Ptah''s heart and on his tongue; the heart conceives all and the tongue speaks all, and gods, towns, food and every craft come from Ptah''s word. When he had made all things Ptah rested, and the gods entered bodies of wood, stone and clay. Last, Osiris is drowned in the water, Isis and Nephthys bring him ashore at Memphis, he enters the earth, and Horus becomes king of Upper and Lower Egypt in his father''s arms.','["埃及", "普塔", "孟菲斯", "创世", "心与舌", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',11,674,'依据大英博物馆藏沙巴卡石（EA 498）按碑文顺序讲述。石板后来被当作磨盘使用，中间大片文字已经磨损，本篇只讲能读的部分，不补写残缺处。碑文说它是古书的复本，学者们对原文的年代意见不一，有人认为写于古王国，也有人认为就是第二十五王朝的作品；本篇不替它定年。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.ugaritic.baal_palace','The palace of Baal: El, Athirat and the house of silver and gold','巴力的宫殿：伊勒、阿西拉特与银金之屋','MYTHIC_NARRATIVE','civ.ugaritic','战胜海神雅姆以后，风暴之神巴力在宴会上饮酒，女战神阿娜特在山谷中大战，然后洗净双手。巴力派使者请阿娜特来到萨方山，告诉她自己的苦恼：众神都有房子，唯独巴力没有。阿娜特闯进众神之父伊勒的住所，威胁要让他的白发流血，却没能得到允许。巴力请工匠之神科塔尔-瓦-哈西斯用金银打造宝座、桌子和碗盏，作为礼物送给众神之母阿西拉特。阿西拉特在海边纺线，起初以为巴力和阿娜特来杀她的儿子，看见金银才高兴起来。她骑着驴去见伊勒，伊勒笑着请她吃喝，问她是不是想念他的爱；阿西拉特说：我们的王是强大的巴力。伊勒终于答应：为巴力建一座房子吧。科塔尔要给房子开一扇窗，巴力起初不肯；大火烧了六天，银子化成板、金子化成砖，宫殿建成。巴力征服了许多城市，回来后答应开窗，从云中的裂缝里发出神圣的雷声，大地震动，然后派使者去向死神穆特宣告他的王权。','After his victory over Yamm the Sea, the storm god Baal feasts, while the warrior goddess Anat fights in the valley and then washes her hands. Baal sends messengers to bring Anat to Mount Saphon and tells her his grief: every god has a house, but Baal has none. Anat bursts in on El, father of the gods, threatening to make his grey hair run with blood, but wins no consent. Baal has the craftsman god Kothar-wa-Khasis forge a throne, a table and bowls of silver and gold as gifts for Athirat, mother of the gods. Athirat, spinning by the sea, at first fears that Baal and Anat have come to kill her sons, then rejoices at the gold and silver. She rides her donkey to El, who laughs and offers her food and drink and asks if she longs for his love; Athirat says: our king is Mightiest Baal. At last El agrees: let a house be built for Baal. Kothar wants to put a window in it, and Baal at first refuses; a fire burns six days, silver turns to plates and gold to bricks, and the palace is complete. Baal conquers many cities, returns, agrees to the window, sends his holy voice through a rift in the clouds so that the earth quakes, and sends messengers to Mot, Death, to declare his kingship.','["乌加里特", "巴力", "伊勒", "阿西拉特", "阿娜特", "宫殿", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',14,681,'依据拉斯沙姆拉出土的巴力史诗泥板 KTU 1.3 与 1.4，按栏次顺序讲述；两块泥板都有残缺，栏次与诗行的划分据现代学者的整理，残缺处只说明而不补写。阿西拉特即后世文献中的亚舍拉，本篇按乌加里特原文称她为阿西拉特。原有的巴力与雅姆、巴力与穆特两个故事分别讲述此前和此后的泥板。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.sumerian.inana_ebih','Inana and Ebiḫ: the mountain that would not bow','伊南娜与埃比赫：不肯低头的山','DIVINE_COMBAT','civ.sumerian','这首苏美尔颂歌先赞美伊南娜的可怖：她披着恐怖，在战斗中奔驰，在天上和地上像狮子一样吼叫。接着，伊南娜说出她的愤怒：她在天地间巡行，来到埃比赫山，这座山却没有向她低头，没有把鼻子贴在地上，没有用嘴唇亲吻尘土。她发誓要让恐怖充满这座高耸的山脉。她穿上庄严的服饰，来到天神安的面前，向父亲诉说，请他允许她去毁灭埃比赫。安却警告她：这座山令众神的居所都充满恐惧，它的果实丰美，林中满是狮子和野牛，你这个小女儿要去做什么？伊南娜怒不可遏，打开了武库的大门，带着风暴和洪水冲向埃比赫，把它毁灭。最后，她站在山的废墟上宣告：正因为你高耸、美丽，却不肯向我低头，我才杀死了你。诗以对伊南娜的赞美结束。','This Sumerian hymn first praises Inana''s terror: clad in fear, she rushes into battle and roars like a lion in heaven and on earth. Then Inana tells her anger: walking through heaven and earth she came to the mountain range Ebiḫ, but it did not bow to her, did not put its nose to the ground nor rub its lips in the dust. She vows to fill the soaring range with her terror. Putting on her majestic garments, she goes before An, the sky god, and asks her father''s leave to destroy Ebiḫ. But An warns her: this mountain has spread terror even over the dwellings of the gods; its fruits are rich, its forests full of lions and wild bulls — what is my little one taking on? Inana, in fury, throws open the gate of her arsenal, rushes on Ebiḫ with storm and flood, and destroys it. Last, standing on the ruin, she declares: because you were lofty and beautiful yet would not bow to me, I have killed you. The poem ends in praise of Inana.','["苏美尔", "伊南娜", "安", "埃比赫", "神的战斗", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',9,691,'依据牛津大学苏美尔文学电子文本语料库（ETCSL）所收《伊南娜与埃比赫》合成文本，按段落顺序讲述。这首诗由多块古巴比伦时期的泥板拼合而成，个别诗行残缺或意义不明，本篇只讲能读通的部分。后世传统把它归于阿卡德公主、乌尔的女祭司恩赫杜安娜，作者归属尚有争议。埃比赫通常被认为是今伊拉克的哈姆林山。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z'),
('story.chinese.leigong_leixu','Leigong: the Han image of the thunder god and Wang Chong''s rebuttal','雷公：汉代人画中的雷神与王充的反驳','TRADITION_OVERVIEW','civ.chinese','东汉思想家王充在《论衡·雷虚》里，记下了他那个时代人们对雷的种种看法，然后一一加以反驳。当时的人们相信：雷电劈断大树、毁坏房屋，是上天来取龙；雷电打死人，是因为那人有不为人知的过错，比如给人吃了不干净的食物，上天发怒，就用雷把他打死，隆隆的雷声就是天发怒的声音。画工们画雷的样子，是一串连在一起的鼓，又画一个像力士一样的人，叫做雷公，左手拉着连鼓，右手举着槌子，像在敲打的样子。王充指出，雷公既然没有翅膀，就不可能在天上飞；他又举出五条证据，说明雷其实是火：被雷击死的人须发烧焦、皮肤灼伤，尸体上有火的气味；雷电能烧毁房屋草木。他认为，雷是盛夏时阳气与阴气相争而激发出来的气，就像把水泼进冶炼的炉火里会发出巨响一样。','In the ''Lei Xu'' (''Thunder: the Falsehood'') chapter of his Lunheng, the Eastern Han thinker Wang Chong records the beliefs of his day about thunder and refutes them one by one. People believed that when thunder split trees and wrecked houses, Heaven was taking a dragon; when it killed a man, it was punishing a hidden fault — feeding people unclean food, say — and Heaven in its anger struck him dead, the rumbling being the sound of Heaven''s wrath. Painters drew thunder as a string of linked drums, and beside them a man like a strongman, called Leigong, the Thunder Lord, pulling the drums with his left hand and raising a mallet in his right as if to strike. Wang Chong points out that Leigong, having no wings, could not fly in the sky; and he gives five proofs that thunder is really fire: those killed by it have singed hair and burned skin and smell of fire, and lightning burns houses and plants. Thunder, he argues, is the energy thrown off when yang and yin contend in high summer, just as water poured on a smelting fire bursts with a roar.','["中国", "雷公", "论衡", "王充", "雷神", "长篇"]','SOURCE_BACKED','PUBLIC_CONTEXT',7,695,'依据王充《论衡·雷虚》按论述顺序讲述，引用的古文只作为讲述的依据，正文用白话。这一篇是汉代人关于雷神信仰与绘画的重要见证，可它是王充为了反驳而记录的，所以本篇同时讲出当时的信仰与王充的批评，不替任何一方下结论；《山海经》雷泽雷神与后世道教、民间的雷部诸神另有记录，不并入。','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z','2026-10-24T22:00:00Z');

